      "content": "UBI is often criticized for its massive cost, which would necessitate crippling tax hikes or unsustainable national debt. Furthermore, opponents argue that guaranteed income disincentivizes work, leading to a decline in labor participation and economic productivity. A strong rebuttal is to point out that UBI is a fiscally irresponsible fantasy that punishes the productive members of society to support those who choose not to contribute.",
      "source": "target",
